    "font" : "SFRM1200",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Finally, we proceed to the main result of this section. We show that if G is a nontrivial (k,g,s)-multipole with s ≤ (k − 2)g, then it cannot happen that |G| ≤ b1(k,g,s). Thus, we obtain a nontrivial lower bound on the size of G."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 5,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 56.693, 701.67, 538.583, 731.204 ],
    "font" : "SFRM1200",
    "font size" : 11.955,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "Theorem 9. Let G be a nontrivial (k,g,s)-multipole for some k ≥ 3, g ≥ 5 and s ≤ (k − 2)g. Then"
  }, {
    "type" : "list",
    "pdfua_tag" : "L",
    "id" : 7,
